  "worldAbout": {
    "title": "Godmode Village",
    "what": "A hand-built village of distinctive places: pondside tea rooms, shops, a chapel and bell tower, a stacked-book library, a crescent glass café, a zigzag art gallery and a treehouse cluster.",
    "tour": "Village Square is the southeast meeting place, bordered by the bakery, bookshop, tea shop and florist. North are the clockmaker’s townhouse and chapel, then the library and Crescent Café. West are the outdoor cinema and Zigzag Gallery; the treehouses stand farther northwest. Southwest, the Teahouse overlooks a pond crossed by wooden market walkways. The lighthouse and keeper’s cottage stand east of the water. Knoll Cottage is the hilltop home east of the square."
